<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/6th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siege of Tyre (585–572 BCE)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 585 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> · Also known as 13-year siege of the island fortress of Tyre</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyre">Tyre</a> was a long siege of the Phoenician island city of Tyre by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nebuchadnezzar-ii">Nebuchadnezzar II</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaldean-empire">Chaldean Empire</a>, begun c. 585 BCE. According to the Chaldean Empire profile, it lasted thirteen years. It illustrated both the empire's ambition and the limits of its siege technology against a maritime target.</p></div>
